# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — never commit a real key
# (Rules.md: the key must never reach a tracked file).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# POST /advisory returns 503 with an explanatory message while this is unset,
# and GET /health reports advisory_ready: false. The rest of the API
# (/surge-zone, /exposure, /routes, /allocation) works without it.

GEMINI_API_KEY=

# The mobile app has its own template at `mobile/.env.example` — Expo reads
# `.env` from the directory holding app.json, so the app's variables must live
# there, not in this file.
